The following test files in Cassandra's
test/unit/org/apache/cassandra/cql3/validation/entities directory, which
this directory mirrors, were not translated:

* UFIdentificationTest.java: checks which functions Cassandra's internal
  statement objects report as used by a statement (CQLStatement's
  getFunctions()), which can't be observed through CQL.

* UFSecurityTest.java: checks the sandbox that restricts what Java
  user-defined functions may do (forbidden classes, time limits). Scylla
  does not support Java user-defined functions.

* UFVerifierTest.java: checks Cassandra's verifier of the byte code of Java
  user-defined functions. Scylla does not support Java user-defined
  functions.

* VirtualTableTest.java: registers test virtual tables implemented in Java
  through Cassandra's internal virtual table registry, and then queries
  them. These test tables can't be created through CQL.

Note also that the tests of user-defined functions which were translated
(uf_test.py, uf_java_test.py, uf_auth_test.py, uf_types_test.py and others)
use functions written in Java when running on Cassandra and in Lua when
running on Scylla.
